= Breaking News From Afganistan

The Doha accords negotiated by former President Trump was meant to bring an end to Americas longest war. May 2021 was agreed upon as the date for American forces to leave Afganistan, in exchange for confirmation by the Taliban that they would not allow terrorist operations in Afganistan and that they would in good faith continue negotiations towards a power sharing agreement with the Afgani government.

As the date of the withdrawal came closer and closer, national security advisors to Sanders requested he extend the withdrawal deadline stating that America could not effectively evacuate its equipment and men in Afganistan in a orderly fasion by the May deadline, yet we chose to ignore them and not extend the deadline. The Taliban launched a massive offensive in April, and the morale of the Afgani army seemingly collapsed at the realization that America would not be there to help them. Despite pentagon experts predictions that the Afgani national army could last a few months minimum during the withdrawal process, it seems the Afgani army was plagued with more corruption and morale issues then we previously thought.

The result has been complete and utter chaos. Taliban troops surrounded Kabul before American troops had fully evacuated, leading to a last minute military operation by NATO to secure a airlift of its citizens, military men, diplomats, and equipment out of Afganistan. Yet the rushed operation has lead to the Taliban to capture billions of dollars of US equipment, which the military did not have time to disable. The chaos of the massive airlift also lead to a suicide bombing killing nearly a dozen American troops.

- @fuck_our_lifes

@fuck_our_lifes
